    {
      "text": "5.2. Selecting a set of priors. To expand the linear random eﬀects model into a robust Bayesian",
      "bbox": [
        110.16099548339844,
        420.9959411621094,
        538.5803833007812,
        429.84271240234375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "framework, we consider a set of prior distributions for µ and τµ.",
      "bbox": [
        110.16099548339844,
        432.950927734375,
        389.7356262207031,
        442.7128601074219
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "There are several methods to elicit priors from experts [32, 19, 20, 18], but there is no obvious",
      "bbox": [
        122.11602783203125,
        444.90692138671875,
        538.592529296875,
        453.7536926269531
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "alternative to specify a set of priors. The approach that we use to specify a set of priors for multiple",
      "bbox": [
        110.16102600097656,
        456.8619079589844,
        538.6024780273438,
        465.70867919921875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "parameters is chosen to illustrate robust Bayesian analysis with IIS and MCMC sampling, and other",
      "bbox": [
        110.16102600097656,
        468.81689453125,
        538.6026000976562,
        477.6636657714844
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "approaches could have been used as well. The prior distributions for each parameter are assumed",
      "bbox": [
        110.16102600097656,
        480.7718811035156,
        538.5925903320312,
        489.61865234375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "to belong to the same family of probability distributions (eq. 30 and eq. 31), but with diﬀerent",
      "bbox": [
        110.16102600097656,
        492.72686767578125,
        538.6424560546875,
        501.5736389160156
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "hyperparameters. In order to consider interaction between parameters, the speciﬁcation of priors is",
      "bbox": [
        110.16102600097656,
        504.682861328125,
        538.5928344726562,
        513.5296630859375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "made using an approach similar to prior predictive check [9, 38]. A compact set of hyperparameters",
      "bbox": [
        110.16102600097656,
        516.6378173828125,
        538.592529296875,
        525.484619140625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "is selected by comparing the distribution of the intervention eﬀect for a random study conditional",
      "bbox": [
        110.16102600097656,
        528.5927734375,
        538.6226196289062,
        537.4395751953125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "on the hyperparameters δ∗|µ, τµ to an elicited range R.",
      "bbox": [
        110.16102600097656,
        538.6165161132812,
        350.88861083984375,
        550.8886108398438
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The selection of a set of priors can be summarized as:",
      "bbox": [
        122.11601257324219,
        552.5028076171875,
        356.86480712890625,
        561.349609375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "(1) Specify a range R where the eﬀect size of a randomly selected study is expected to fall with",
      "bbox": [
        127.09801483154297,
